# TEMDD performance contract v0.1

Correctness precedes throughput. The semantic kernel performs finite event transitions and does not poll. Fixed, proven relations should be lowerable to C90/M68000 paths; inspectable dynamic relations may remain in Smalltalk/Python. Optimizations must preserve canonical IR behavior and pass differential vectors. Caches are transport/runtime optimizations and cannot change evidence freshness, authority, exact-subject identity, or effect-readback requirements.
